course: dictionary
lesson: 6180
title: Minute: a short time, or very small
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A minute is a unit of time. Sixty minutes make one hour, so a minute is one sixtieth of an hour. «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00.» Those two numbers add up to 45 minutes, so he has to start getting ready early.
explain: People also say minute to mean a very short time, like «Wait a minute». The meaning changes with the words around it. In «Wait a minute», nobody is counting exactly, and the speaker means "just a moment". Use the context to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Minute can also be an adjective, said «my-NEWT», meaning very, very small. A minute detail is so small that you might miss it. The sentence tells you which one you need: the time sense usually has a number next to it, like "20 minutes".
fact: A minute is one sixtieth of an hour.
fact: One minute has 60 seconds, and one hour has 60 minutes.
fact: The long hand of a clock is called the minute hand.
fact: «At the last minute» means at the very latest moment, just before something happens.
fact: «Minute» (said «my-NEWT») means very, very small.
exercise: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes.» How long do they take altogether? | 60 minutes | 25 minutes | *45 minutes | 20 minutes
exercise: «Wait a minute, I am nearly ready.» What does a minute mean here? | A long, slow walk | Exactly sixty hours | *A very short time | A tiny insect
exercise: «A hedgehog may breathe only a few times a minute in winter.» What does this tell you? | It breathes faster than a human | *It breathes very slowly, only a few breaths in one minute | It breathes once every hour exactly | It never breathes at all
test: How many minutes are there in one hour? | 100 | *60 | 12 | 30
test: Which word describes something very, very small? | Glum | Huge | *Minute | Ancient
exam: «A hot drink can still scald a small child badly fifteen minutes after it was made.» What does fifteen minutes mean? | Fifteen days | Fifteen seconds | *Fifteen lots of sixty seconds | Fifteen hours
